    <article class="docs-prose">
      <h1 id="stage-13-metadata-and-index" class="group scroll-mt-20">Stage 13: Metadata and index<a href="#stage-13-metadata-and-index" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h1>
      <p>Add author, date, audience, keyword, and index metadata to the topics. Place it in <code>&lt;prolog&gt;</code>, between the short description and the body. Add publication metadata to the map's <code>&lt;topicmeta&gt;</code>.</p>
      <p>Configure a metadata policy in <code>.dogsbay/config.xml</code> to require keywords on topics and creation dates on tasks. The examples show each topic type; expand the remaining examples to apply the same structure.</p>
      <p><strong>Optional module.</strong> See <a href="/dogsbay-xml-dita-tutorial-docs/start-here/learning-path">Choose a learning path</a> for the starting checkpoint and the next core lesson.</p>
      <p><strong>Time:</strong> about 40 minutes. <strong>You need:</strong> stage 12 complete.</p>
      <p>Recorded diagnostic examples below come from earlier runs. File counts, paths, and stage numbers can differ. Run the gate for your current checkout.</p>
      <h2 id="step-1-the-prolog-of-a-concept" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 1: The prolog of a concept<a href="#step-1-the-prolog-of-a-concept" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><strong><code>topics/what-is-audacity.dita</code></strong> This one carries every element the stage uses.
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/what-is-audacity.dita\n+++ b/topics/what-is-audacity.dita\n@@ -4,6 +4,29 @@\n \u003cconcept id=\"what-is-audacity\">\n   \u003ctitle>What is \u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/>?\u003c/title>\n   \u003cshortdesc>\u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> is a free, open-source audio editor and recorder for Windows, macOS and Linux.\u003c/shortdesc>\n+  \u003cprolog>\n+    \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n+    \u003ccopyright>\n+      \u003ccopyryear year=\"2026\"/>\n+      \u003ccopyrholder>DogsBay Ltd.\u003c/copyrholder>\n+    \u003c/copyright>\n+    \u003ccritdates>\n+      \u003ccreated date=\"2026-01-10\"/>\n+    \u003c/critdates>\n+    \u003cmetadata>\n+      \u003caudience type=\"user\" experiencelevel=\"novice\"/>\n+      \u003ccategory>concept\u003c/category>\n+      \u003ckeywords>\n+        \u003ckeyword>Audacity\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>audio editor\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>open source\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003cindexterm>Audacity\u003cindexterm>overview\u003c/indexterm>\u003c/indexterm>\n+        \u003cindexterm>audio editor\u003cindex-see>Audacity\u003c/index-see>\u003c/indexterm>\n+      \u003c/keywords>\n+    \u003c/metadata>\n+    \u003cresourceid appname=\"audacity-help\" id=\"intro\"/>\n+    \u003cdata name=\"reading-time\" value=\"2 min\"/>\n+  \u003c/prolog>\n   \u003cconbody>\n     \u003cp>\u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> records live audio, imports and exports the common audio formats, and edits sound with cut, copy, paste and a library of effects.\n     It is free to download and use, and it runs on Windows, macOS and Linux.\u003c/p>"} lang="diff" title="topics/what-is-audacity.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the order</strong> The children of <code>&lt;prolog&gt;</code> come in a fixed order: <code>&lt;author&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;source&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;publisher&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;copyright&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;critdates&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;permissions&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;metadata&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;resourceid&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;data&gt;</code>. Skip any, but do not reorder them. <code>&lt;resourceid&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;data&gt;</code> come after <code>&lt;metadata&gt;</code>, not inside it; put them inside and the file does not validate.
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the elements</strong>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;author type="creator"&gt;</code> names who wrote the topic; <code>type</code> may also be <code>contributor</code>.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;copyright&gt;</code> holds a <code>&lt;copyryear year="…"/&gt;</code> and a <code>&lt;copyrholder&gt;</code>. Only this topic carries one; the map's copyright covers the guide.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;critdates&gt;</code> holds <code>&lt;created date="…"/&gt;</code> and, in the topics that have been revised, <code>&lt;revised modified="…"/&gt;</code>. Dates are <code>YYYY-MM-DD</code>.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;metadata&gt;</code> groups the classification: <code>&lt;audience type="user" experiencelevel="novice"/&gt;</code>, a <code>&lt;category&gt;</code>, and <code>&lt;keywords&gt;</code>.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;keywords&gt;</code> holds <code>&lt;keyword&gt;</code>s, which the HTML5 output writes into a <code>&lt;meta name="keywords"&gt;</code> tag, and <code>&lt;indexterm&gt;</code>s, which it does not render: an index is a print artifact, and the PDF in stage 19 builds one from them.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;resourceid appname="…" id="…"/&gt;</code> is an identifier for another system, here a help system that will link to this topic. <code>&lt;data name="…" value="…"/&gt;</code> is a named property with no defined meaning; a processor or a house rule can use it.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-2-the-prologs-of-the-other-topics" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 2: The prologs of the other topics<a href="#step-2-the-prologs-of-the-other-topics" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><strong><code>topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita</code></strong> A revision date, and three index-term forms.
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita\n+++ b/topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita\n@@ -4,6 +4,31 @@\n \u003cconcept id=\"what-is-digital-audio\">\n   \u003ctitle>What is digital audio?\u003c/title>\n   \u003cshortdesc>Digital audio is sound stored as numbers: samples taken thousands of times a second at a chosen precision.\u003c/shortdesc>\n+  \u003cprolog>\n+    \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n+    \u003ccritdates>\n+      \u003ccreated date=\"2026-01-10\"/>\n+      \u003crevised modified=\"2026-03-02\"/>\n+    \u003c/critdates>\n+    \u003cmetadata>\n+      \u003caudience type=\"user\" experiencelevel=\"novice\"/>\n+      \u003ccategory>concept\u003c/category>\n+      \u003ckeywords>\n+        \u003ckeyword>digital audio\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>sample rate\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>bit depth\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>waveform\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>decibel\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003cindexterm>digital audio\u003c/indexterm>\n+        \u003cindexterm>sample rate\u003c/indexterm>\n+        \u003cindexterm>bit depth\u003c/indexterm>\n+        \u003cindexterm>waveform\u003c/indexterm>\n+        \u003cindexterm>decibel\u003cindex-see-also>amplitude\u003c/index-see-also>\u003c/indexterm>\n+        \u003cindexterm>amplitude\u003c/indexterm>\n+        \u003cindexterm>\u003cindex-sort-as>clipping\u003c/index-sort-as>Clipping (distortion)\u003c/indexterm>\n+      \u003c/keywords>\n+    \u003c/metadata>\n+  \u003c/prolog>\n   \u003cconbody>\n     \u003cp>Digital audio is sound that has been converted into a numerical representation.\n     A few key concepts help you make better recordings and edits."} lang="diff" title="topics/what-is-digital-audio.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><strong><code>topics/installing-audacity.dita</code></strong> A nested index term.
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/installing-audacity.dita\n+++ b/topics/installing-audacity.dita\n@@ -4,6 +4,25 @@\n \u003ctask id=\"installing-audacity\">\n   \u003ctitle>Installing \u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/>\u003c/title>\n   \u003cshortdesc>Download \u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> from the official website, or install it with your package manager, and launch it once to finish setup.\u003c/shortdesc>\n+  \u003cprolog>\n+    \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n+    \u003ccritdates>\n+      \u003ccreated date=\"2026-01-12\"/>\n+    \u003c/critdates>\n+    \u003cmetadata>\n+      \u003caudience type=\"user\" experiencelevel=\"novice\"/>\n+      \u003ccategory>installation\u003c/category>\n+      \u003ckeywords>\n+        \u003ckeyword>install\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>download\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>Windows\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>macOS\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>Linux\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003cindexterm>installing\u003cindexterm>Windows\u003c/indexterm>\u003cindexterm>macOS\u003c/indexterm>\u003cindexterm>Linux\u003c/indexterm>\u003c/indexterm>\n+        \u003cindexterm>download\u003c/indexterm>\n+      \u003c/keywords>\n+    \u003c/metadata>\n+  \u003c/prolog>\n   \u003ctaskbody>\n     \u003cprereq>\n       \u003cp>You need about 250 MB of free disk space and an account that can install software.\u003c/p>"} lang="diff" title="topics/installing-audacity.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><strong><code>topics/supported-audio-formats.dita</code></strong> A revision date and an index redirect.
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/supported-audio-formats.dita\n+++ b/topics/supported-audio-formats.dita\n@@ -4,6 +4,26 @@\n \u003creference id=\"supported-audio-formats\">\n   \u003ctitle>Supported audio formats\u003c/title>\n   \u003cshortdesc>The audio formats \u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> imports and exports, and when to use each one.\u003c/shortdesc>\n+  \u003cprolog>\n+    \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n+    \u003ccritdates>\n+      \u003ccreated date=\"2026-01-22\"/>\n+      \u003crevised modified=\"2026-02-14\"/>\n+    \u003c/critdates>\n+    \u003cmetadata>\n+      \u003caudience type=\"user\" experiencelevel=\"novice\"/>\n+      \u003ccategory>reference\u003c/category>\n+      \u003ckeywords>\n+        \u003ckeyword>audio formats\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>lossless\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>lossy\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>MP3\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>FLAC\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003cindexterm>audio formats\u003cindexterm>lossless\u003c/indexterm>\u003cindexterm>lossy\u003c/indexterm>\u003c/indexterm>\n+        \u003cindexterm>codecs\u003cindex-see>audio formats\u003c/index-see>\u003c/indexterm>\n+      \u003c/keywords>\n+    \u003c/metadata>\n+  \u003c/prolog>\n   \u003crefbody>\n     \u003csection>\n       \u003cp>\u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/> imports and exports audio in several formats.\n@@ -46,7 +66,9 @@\n           \u003c/row>\n           \u003crow>\n             \u003centry>MP3\u003c/entry>\n-            \u003centry>\u003cterm keyref=\"gl-compression\">Compressed\u003c/term>\u003c/entry>\n+            \u003centry>\n+              \u003cterm keyref=\"gl-compression\">Compressed\u003c/term>\n+            \u003c/entry>\n             \u003centry>Lossy\u003c/entry>\n             \u003centry>Widely supported, small files.\n             Needs the \u003ci>LAME\u003c/i> encoder, bundled since version 2.3.2."} lang="diff" title="topics/supported-audio-formats.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the index terms</strong>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;indexterm&gt;</code> is an entry in the index. An <code>&lt;indexterm&gt;</code> inside another is a sub-entry: <code>installing</code> with <code>Windows</code>, <code>macOS</code> and <code>Linux</code> under it.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;index-see&gt;</code> inside an entry redirects it: "codecs, <em>see</em> audio formats". The entry with <code>&lt;index-see&gt;</code> has no page of its own.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;index-see-also&gt;</code> adds a cross-reference under an entry that does have pages: "decibel … <em>see also</em> amplitude".</li>
      <li><code>&lt;index-sort-as&gt;</code> gives the text to sort by when it differs from the text shown: <code>Clipping (distortion)</code> sorts as <code>clipping</code>.</li>
      <li><code>project-health</code> checks the index. Change the redirect to <code>audio format</code> and it reports, under <em>Index redirects to nothing</em>, <code>"codecs" see "audio format"</code>.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit the remaining five tasks</strong> Same shape: author, <code>&lt;created&gt;</code>, audience, category, keywords and index terms. The noise task is the one topic for an intermediate audience.
      <CollapsibleAlert variant="note" title="topics/exporting-audio.dita" class="my-4">
        <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/exporting-audio.dita\n+++ b/topics/exporting-audio.dita\n@@ -4,6 +4,25 @@\n \u003ctask id=\"exporting-audio\">\n   \u003ctitle>Exporting audio\u003c/title>\n   \u003cshortdesc>Export a finished project as a WAV, MP3, OGG or FLAC file that other programs and devices can play.\u003c/shortdesc>\n+  \u003cprolog>\n+    \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n+    \u003ccritdates>\n+      \u003ccreated date=\"2026-01-22\"/>\n+    \u003c/critdates>\n+    \u003cmetadata>\n+      \u003caudience type=\"user\" experiencelevel=\"novice\"/>\n+      \u003ccategory>exporting\u003c/category>\n+      \u003ckeywords>\n+        \u003ckeyword>export\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>MP3\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>WAV\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>FLAC\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>OGG\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003cindexterm>exporting\u003c/indexterm>\n+        \u003cindexterm>audio formats\u003cindexterm>MP3\u003c/indexterm>\u003cindexterm>WAV\u003c/indexterm>\u003c/indexterm>\n+      \u003c/keywords>\n+    \u003c/metadata>\n+  \u003c/prolog>\n   \u003ctaskbody>\n     \u003cprereq>\n       \u003cp>Finish editing and save the project."} lang="diff" title="topics/exporting-audio.dita" />
      </CollapsibleAlert>
      <CollapsibleAlert variant="note" title="topics/preparing-to-record.dita" class="my-4">
        <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/preparing-to-record.dita\n+++ b/topics/preparing-to-record.dita\n@@ -4,6 +4,24 @@\n \u003ctask id=\"preparing-to-record\">\n   \u003ctitle>Preparing to record\u003c/title>\n   \u003cshortdesc>Checks to make in any order before you press Record: input level, sample rate and disk space.\u003c/shortdesc>\n+  \u003cprolog>\n+    \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n+    \u003ccritdates>\n+      \u003ccreated date=\"2026-01-15\"/>\n+    \u003c/critdates>\n+    \u003cmetadata>\n+      \u003caudience type=\"user\" experiencelevel=\"novice\"/>\n+      \u003ccategory>recording\u003c/category>\n+      \u003ckeywords>\n+        \u003ckeyword>recording\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>levels\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>sample rate\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>disk space\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003cindexterm>recording\u003cindexterm>preparing\u003c/indexterm>\u003cindexterm>levels\u003c/indexterm>\u003c/indexterm>\n+        \u003cindexterm>clipping\u003c/indexterm>\n+      \u003c/keywords>\n+    \u003c/metadata>\n+  \u003c/prolog>\n   \u003ctaskbody>\n     \u003ccontext>\n       \u003cp>None of these checks depends on another, so do them in whatever order suits you.\u003c/p>"} lang="diff" title="topics/preparing-to-record.dita" />
      </CollapsibleAlert>
      <CollapsibleAlert variant="note" title="topics/recording-your-first-track.dita" class="my-4">
        <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/recording-your-first-track.dita\n+++ b/topics/recording-your-first-track.dita\n@@ -4,6 +4,24 @@\n \u003ctask id=\"recording-your-first-track\">\n   \u003ctitle>Recording your first track\u003c/title>\n   \u003cshortdesc>Make your first recording in \u003ckeyword keyref=\"product-name\"/>: pick a microphone, record, stop and play it back.\u003c/shortdesc>\n+  \u003cprolog>\n+    \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n+    \u003ccritdates>\n+      \u003ccreated date=\"2026-01-15\"/>\n+    \u003c/critdates>\n+    \u003cmetadata>\n+      \u003caudience type=\"user\" experiencelevel=\"novice\"/>\n+      \u003ccategory>recording\u003c/category>\n+      \u003ckeywords>\n+        \u003ckeyword>recording\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>microphone\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>Device Toolbar\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003cindexterm>recording\u003cindexterm>first track\u003c/indexterm>\u003c/indexterm>\n+        \u003cindexterm>microphone\u003c/indexterm>\n+        \u003cindexterm>Device Toolbar\u003c/indexterm>\n+      \u003c/keywords>\n+    \u003c/metadata>\n+  \u003c/prolog>\n   \u003ctaskbody>\n     \u003ccontext>\n       \u003cp>This task walks you through making your first audio recording."} lang="diff" title="topics/recording-your-first-track.dita" />
      </CollapsibleAlert>
      <CollapsibleAlert variant="note" title="topics/removing-background-noise.dita" class="my-4">
        <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/removing-background-noise.dita\n+++ b/topics/removing-background-noise.dita\n@@ -4,6 +4,24 @@\n \u003ctask id=\"removing-background-noise\">\n   \u003ctitle>Removing background noise\u003c/title>\n   \u003cshortdesc>Take a noise profile from a quiet section, then apply Noise Reduction to the whole track to remove hum, hiss and fan noise.\u003c/shortdesc>\n+  \u003cprolog>\n+    \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n+    \u003ccritdates>\n+      \u003ccreated date=\"2026-01-20\"/>\n+    \u003c/critdates>\n+    \u003cmetadata>\n+      \u003caudience type=\"user\" experiencelevel=\"intermediate\"/>\n+      \u003ccategory>editing\u003c/category>\n+      \u003ckeywords>\n+        \u003ckeyword>noise reduction\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>noise profile\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>effects\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003cindexterm>noise reduction\u003c/indexterm>\n+        \u003cindexterm>effects\u003cindexterm>Noise Reduction\u003c/indexterm>\u003c/indexterm>\n+        \u003cindexterm>hum\u003cindex-see>noise reduction\u003c/index-see>\u003c/indexterm>\n+      \u003c/keywords>\n+    \u003c/metadata>\n+  \u003c/prolog>\n   \u003ctaskbody>\n     \u003ccontext>\n       \u003cp>Background noise such as hum from electronics, hiss from a microphone or fan noise degrades a recording."} lang="diff" title="topics/removing-background-noise.dita" />
      </CollapsibleAlert>
      <CollapsibleAlert variant="note" title="topics/trimming-audio.dita" class="my-4">
        <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/trimming-audio.dita\n+++ b/topics/trimming-audio.dita\n@@ -4,6 +4,25 @@\n \u003ctask id=\"trimming-audio\">\n   \u003ctitle>Trimming audio\u003c/title>\n   \u003cshortdesc>Remove silence, false starts and mistakes by selecting a region of the waveform and deleting it.\u003c/shortdesc>\n+  \u003cprolog>\n+    \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n+    \u003ccritdates>\n+      \u003ccreated date=\"2026-01-18\"/>\n+    \u003c/critdates>\n+    \u003cmetadata>\n+      \u003caudience type=\"user\" experiencelevel=\"novice\"/>\n+      \u003ccategory>editing\u003c/category>\n+      \u003ckeywords>\n+        \u003ckeyword>trimming\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>editing\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>delete\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>selection\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003cindexterm>trimming\u003c/indexterm>\n+        \u003cindexterm>editing\u003cindexterm>trimming\u003c/indexterm>\u003c/indexterm>\n+        \u003cindexterm>selection\u003c/indexterm>\n+      \u003c/keywords>\n+    \u003c/metadata>\n+  \u003c/prolog>\n   \u003ctaskbody>\n     \u003ccontext>\n       \u003cp>Trimming removes unwanted audio from the start, end or middle of a track."} lang="diff" title="topics/trimming-audio.dita" />
      </CollapsibleAlert>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-3-the-glossary-and-the-shared-topics" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 3: The glossary and the shared topics<a href="#step-3-the-glossary-and-the-shared-topics" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><strong><code>topics/glossary/audio-units.dita</code></strong> The group gets a prolog of its own, and so does each entry inside it.
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/glossary/audio-units.dita\n+++ b/topics/glossary/audio-units.dita\n@@ -3,9 +3,28 @@\n \n \u003cglossgroup id=\"audio-units\">\n   \u003ctitle>Units\u003c/title>\n+  \u003cprolog>\n+    \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n+    \u003cmetadata>\n+      \u003ckeywords>\n+        \u003ckeyword>units\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>glossary\u003c/keyword>\n+      \u003c/keywords>\n+    \u003c/metadata>\n+  \u003c/prolog>\n   \u003cglossentry id=\"gl-decibel\">\n     \u003cglossterm>decibel\u003c/glossterm>\n     \u003cglossdef>A logarithmic unit for the ratio between two levels. In audio editing, 0 dB is the loudest level a file can hold, and quieter sounds are negative.\u003c/glossdef>\n+    \u003cprolog>\n+      \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n+      \u003cmetadata>\n+        \u003ckeywords>\n+          \u003ckeyword>decibel\u003c/keyword>\n+          \u003ckeyword>glossary\u003c/keyword>\n+          \u003cindexterm>decibel\u003c/indexterm>\n+        \u003c/keywords>\n+      \u003c/metadata>\n+    \u003c/prolog>\n     \u003cglossBody>\n       \u003cglossSurfaceForm>decibel (dB)\u003c/glossSurfaceForm>\n       \u003cglossAlt>\n@@ -16,6 +35,16 @@\n   \u003cglossentry id=\"gl-hertz\">\n     \u003cglossterm>hertz\u003c/glossterm>\n     \u003cglossdef>Cycles per second. Sample rates are given in hertz: 44,100 Hz means 44,100 samples every second.\u003c/glossdef>\n+    \u003cprolog>\n+      \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n+      \u003cmetadata>\n+        \u003ckeywords>\n+          \u003ckeyword>hertz\u003c/keyword>\n+          \u003ckeyword>glossary\u003c/keyword>\n+          \u003cindexterm>hertz\u003c/indexterm>\n+        \u003c/keywords>\n+      \u003c/metadata>\n+    \u003c/prolog>\n     \u003cglossBody>\n       \u003cglossSurfaceForm>hertz (Hz)\u003c/glossSurfaceForm>\n       \u003cglossAlt>"} lang="diff" title="topics/glossary/audio-units.dita" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read why the group has one</strong> A <code>&lt;glossgroup&gt;</code> is a topic, and the policy in step 5 says every topic needs a keyword. Give the entries prologs and leave the group without, and <code>project-health</code> reports <code>topics/glossary/audio-units.dita — [error] missing required &lt;keyword&gt;</code>. In a <code>&lt;glossentry&gt;</code> the <code>&lt;prolog&gt;</code> follows <code>&lt;glossdef&gt;</code>, and in a <code>&lt;glossgroup&gt;</code> it follows <code>&lt;title&gt;</code>, before the first entry.
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit the six entry files</strong> Author and keywords, with the term as an index entry. No <code>&lt;created&gt;</code>: the policy requires a date on tasks only.
      <CollapsibleAlert variant="note" title="topics/glossary/g-bit-depth.dita, and the other five alike" class="my-4">
        <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/glossary/g-bit-depth.dita\n+++ b/topics/glossary/g-bit-depth.dita\n@@ -4,4 +4,14 @@\n \u003cglossentry id=\"gl-bit-depth\">\n   \u003cglossterm>Bit depth\u003c/glossterm>\n   \u003cglossdef>The number of bits used to store each sample, which sets how precisely amplitude is recorded. 16-bit audio has 65,536 possible values; 24-bit has over 16 million.\u003c/glossdef>\n+  \u003cprolog>\n+    \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n+    \u003cmetadata>\n+      \u003ckeywords>\n+        \u003ckeyword>Bit depth\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>glossary\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003cindexterm>Bit depth\u003c/indexterm>\n+      \u003c/keywords>\n+    \u003c/metadata>\n+  \u003c/prolog>\n \u003c/glossentry>"} lang="diff" title="topics/glossary/g-bit-depth.dita" />
        <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/glossary/g-clipping.dita\n+++ b/topics/glossary/g-clipping.dita\n@@ -4,4 +4,14 @@\n \u003cglossentry id=\"gl-clipping\">\n   \u003cglossterm>Clipping\u003c/glossterm>\n   \u003cglossdef>Distortion that occurs when a signal exceeds the maximum amplitude the system can represent. Clipped peaks are cut flat and cannot be repaired.\u003c/glossdef>\n+  \u003cprolog>\n+    \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n+    \u003cmetadata>\n+      \u003ckeywords>\n+        \u003ckeyword>Clipping\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>glossary\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003cindexterm>Clipping\u003c/indexterm>\n+      \u003c/keywords>\n+    \u003c/metadata>\n+  \u003c/prolog>\n \u003c/glossentry>"} lang="diff" title="topics/glossary/g-clipping.dita" />
        <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/glossary/g-compression.dita\n+++ b/topics/glossary/g-compression.dita\n@@ -4,4 +4,14 @@\n \u003cglossentry id=\"gl-compression\">\n   \u003cglossterm>Compression\u003c/glossterm>\n   \u003cglossdef>Reducing the dynamic range of audio so that quiet parts are louder and loud parts quieter. Not to be confused with file compression such as MP3.\u003c/glossdef>\n+  \u003cprolog>\n+    \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n+    \u003cmetadata>\n+      \u003ckeywords>\n+        \u003ckeyword>Compression\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>glossary\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003cindexterm>Compression\u003c/indexterm>\n+      \u003c/keywords>\n+    \u003c/metadata>\n+  \u003c/prolog>\n \u003c/glossentry>"} lang="diff" title="topics/glossary/g-compression.dita" />
        <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/glossary/g-normalization.dita\n+++ b/topics/glossary/g-normalization.dita\n@@ -4,4 +4,14 @@\n \u003cglossentry id=\"gl-normalization\">\n   \u003cglossterm>Normalization\u003c/glossterm>\n   \u003cglossdef>Raising or lowering the level of a recording so that its loudest peak sits at a chosen target, giving consistent loudness across clips.\u003c/glossdef>\n+  \u003cprolog>\n+    \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n+    \u003cmetadata>\n+      \u003ckeywords>\n+        \u003ckeyword>Normalization\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>glossary\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003cindexterm>Normalization\u003c/indexterm>\n+      \u003c/keywords>\n+    \u003c/metadata>\n+  \u003c/prolog>\n \u003c/glossentry>"} lang="diff" title="topics/glossary/g-normalization.dita" />
        <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/glossary/g-sample-rate.dita\n+++ b/topics/glossary/g-sample-rate.dita\n@@ -4,4 +4,14 @@\n \u003cglossentry id=\"gl-sample-rate\">\n   \u003cglossterm>Sample rate\u003c/glossterm>\n   \u003cglossdef>The number of audio samples captured per second, measured in hertz. Higher sample rates capture more detail. CD audio uses 44,100 Hz; video production typically uses 48,000 Hz.\u003c/glossdef>\n+  \u003cprolog>\n+    \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n+    \u003cmetadata>\n+      \u003ckeywords>\n+        \u003ckeyword>Sample rate\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>glossary\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003cindexterm>Sample rate\u003c/indexterm>\n+      \u003c/keywords>\n+    \u003c/metadata>\n+  \u003c/prolog>\n \u003c/glossentry>"} lang="diff" title="topics/glossary/g-sample-rate.dita" />
        <CodeBlock code={"--- a/topics/glossary/g-waveform.dita\n+++ b/topics/glossary/g-waveform.dita\n@@ -4,4 +4,14 @@\n \u003cglossentry id=\"gl-waveform\">\n   \u003cglossterm>Waveform\u003c/glossterm>\n   \u003cglossdef>The shape of a sound wave over time, drawn as amplitude against time. Audacity shows each track as a waveform.\u003c/glossdef>\n+  \u003cprolog>\n+    \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n+    \u003cmetadata>\n+      \u003ckeywords>\n+        \u003ckeyword>Waveform\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>glossary\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003cindexterm>Waveform\u003c/indexterm>\n+      \u003c/keywords>\n+    \u003c/metadata>\n+  \u003c/prolog>\n \u003c/glossentry>"} lang="diff" title="topics/glossary/g-waveform.dita" />
      </CollapsibleAlert>
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit the two shared topics</strong> Shared topics are topics too. Their audience is <code>author</code>, because a writer is the only person who reads them, and their category is <code>warehouse</code>.
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/shared/common-notes.dita\n+++ b/shared/common-notes.dita\n@@ -4,6 +4,21 @@\n \u003ctopic id=\"common-notes\">\n   \u003ctitle>Common notes\u003c/title>\n   \u003cshortdesc>Reusable notes, tips and lists that other topics pull in by conref. This topic is a warehouse and is not published on its own.\u003c/shortdesc>\n+  \u003cprolog>\n+    \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n+    \u003ccritdates>\n+      \u003ccreated date=\"2026-01-15\"/>\n+    \u003c/critdates>\n+    \u003cmetadata>\n+      \u003caudience type=\"author\"/>\n+      \u003ccategory>warehouse\u003c/category>\n+      \u003ckeywords>\n+        \u003ckeyword>reuse\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>conref\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>notes\u003c/keyword>\n+      \u003c/keywords>\n+    \u003c/metadata>\n+  \u003c/prolog>\n   \u003cbody>\n     \u003cnote id=\"backup-warning\" type=\"warning\">This effect changes the audio data.\n     Save the project first; you can undo with \u003cuicontrol>Ctrl+Z\u003c/uicontrol> (Windows and Linux) or \u003cuicontrol>Cmd+Z\u003c/uicontrol> (macOS).\u003c/note>"} lang="diff" title="shared/common-notes.dita" />
      <CollapsibleAlert variant="note" title="shared/common-steps.dita" class="my-4">
        <CodeBlock code={"--- a/shared/common-steps.dita\n+++ b/shared/common-steps.dita\n@@ -4,6 +4,21 @@\n \u003ctask id=\"common-steps\">\n   \u003ctitle>Common steps\u003c/title>\n   \u003cshortdesc>Reusable steps that other tasks pull in by conref. This task is a warehouse and is not published on its own.\u003c/shortdesc>\n+  \u003cprolog>\n+    \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n+    \u003ccritdates>\n+      \u003ccreated date=\"2026-01-15\"/>\n+    \u003c/critdates>\n+    \u003cmetadata>\n+      \u003caudience type=\"author\"/>\n+      \u003ccategory>warehouse\u003c/category>\n+      \u003ckeywords>\n+        \u003ckeyword>reuse\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>conref\u003c/keyword>\n+        \u003ckeyword>steps\u003c/keyword>\n+      \u003c/keywords>\n+    \u003c/metadata>\n+  \u003c/prolog>\n   \u003ctaskbody>\n     \u003csteps>\n       \u003cstep id=\"select-region\">"} lang="diff" title="shared/common-steps.dita" />
      </CollapsibleAlert>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-4-metadata-for-the-publication" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 4: Metadata for the publication<a href="#step-4-metadata-for-the-publication" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><strong><code>audacity-guide.ditamap</code></strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/audacity-guide.ditamap\n+++ b/audacity-guide.ditamap\n@@ -5,6 +5,20 @@\n   \u003ctitle>Audacity User Guide\u003c/title>\n   \u003ctopicmeta>\n     \u003cshortdesc>Record, edit and export audio with Audacity, from your first track to a finished file.\u003c/shortdesc>\n+    \u003cauthor type=\"creator\">The Audacity tutorial team\u003c/author>\n+    \u003cpublisher>DogsBay Ltd.\u003c/publisher>\n+    \u003ccopyright>\n+      \u003ccopyryear year=\"2026\"/>\n+      \u003ccopyrholder>DogsBay Ltd.\u003c/copyrholder>\n+    \u003c/copyright>\n+    \u003ccritdates>\n+      \u003ccreated date=\"2026-01-10\"/>\n+    \u003c/critdates>\n+    \u003caudience type=\"user\"/>\n+    \u003ckeywords>\n+      \u003ckeyword>Audacity\u003c/keyword>\n+      \u003ckeyword>audio editing\u003c/keyword>\n+    \u003c/keywords>\n   \u003c/topicmeta>\n \n   \u003cmapref href=\"keydefs-product.ditamap\"/>"} lang="diff" title="audacity-guide.ditamap" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the map metadata</strong> The map's <code>&lt;topicmeta&gt;</code> takes the same elements as a prolog, in the same order, without the <code>&lt;metadata&gt;</code> wrapper: <code>&lt;author&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;publisher&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;copyright&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;critdates&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;audience&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;keywords&gt;</code> sit directly inside it. Map metadata applies to the publication and, for the HTML5 transform, cascades into every page: the <code>&lt;meta name="rights"&gt;</code> tag on each page comes from this copyright.
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <h2 id="step-5-the-metadata-policy-the-readme-and-the-gate" class="group scroll-mt-20">Step 5: The metadata policy, the README and the gate<a href="#step-5-the-metadata-policy-the-readme-and-the-gate" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <Steps>
      <Step>
      <strong>Edit </strong><strong><code>.dogsbay/config.xml</code></strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/.dogsbay/config.xml\n+++ b/.dogsbay/config.xml\n@@ -6,4 +6,9 @@\n   \u003cframework>DITA-OT 4.3.5\u003c/framework>\n   \u003cformat-style indent=\"spaces\" size=\"2\" max-line-width=\"0\" preserve-mixed=\"true\" newline=\"lf\" final-newline=\"true\" preserve-text-breaks=\"true\" preserve-blank-lines=\"true\" text-continuation=\"block\" trim-whitespace=\"true\"/>\n   \u003cdefault-deliverable file=\"project.json\" name=\"full\"/>\n+  \u003cmetadata-policy>\n+    \u003crule topic-type=\"task\" field=\"created\" presence=\"required\" pattern=\"\\d{4}-\\d\\d-\\d\\d\"/>\n+    \u003crule field=\"author\" presence=\"recommended\"/>\n+    \u003crule field=\"keyword\" presence=\"required\"/>\n+  \u003c/metadata-policy>\n \u003c/dogsbay-project>"} lang="diff" title=".dogsbay/config.xml" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Read the rules</strong>
      <ul>
      <li>Each <code>&lt;rule&gt;</code> names a <code>field</code>, a <code>presence</code> and, optionally, a <code>topic-type</code> and a <code>pattern</code>. A missing <code>required</code> field is an error and fails the gate; a missing <code>recommended</code> field is a warning, shown beside a file's errors.</li>
      <li><code>created</code> is required on every task, and must match <code>\d{"{"}4{"}"}-\d\d-\d\d</code>. Concepts, references and glossary entries may leave it out.</li>
      <li><code>author</code> is recommended everywhere. <code>keyword</code> is required everywhere, which is the rule that reaches the glossary group.</li>
      <li><code>project-health</code> applies the policy as one of its checks, so the gate enforces it. The editor reads the same file.</li>
      </ul>
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Change the "You are on" line</strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"--- a/README.md\n+++ b/README.md\n@@ -2,7 +2,7 @@\n \n Build a guide through 27 stages. Maps begin at stage 02; HTML publication begins at stage 03.\n \n-You are on stage 12: glossary.\n+You are on stage 13: metadata and index.\n \n ## Stages\n "} lang="diff" title="README.md" />
      </Step>
      <Step>
      <strong>Format and check</strong>
      <CodeBlock code={"dogsbay-xml format -i topics/*.dita topics/glossary/*.dita shared/*.dita\nscripts/check-stage.sh"} lang="bash" />
      <CodeBlock code={"== validate-project  /home/you/audacity-guide ==\n21 file(s): 21 valid, 0 invalid.\n\n== project-health  /home/you/audacity-guide ==\nRoot map: audacity-guide.ditamap (project config); house rules: none (none configured)\nProject is healthy: valid, no broken references, keys, orphans, or broken element ids.\n\n== build  project.json -> /tmp/check-stage-357688 ==\nall deliverables built\n\nSTAGE OK"} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>Run <code>dita --project=project.json</code> to build in the project directory. In <code>out/full/topics/what-is-audacity.html</code> the <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> now carries <code>&lt;meta name="keywords" content="Audacity, audio editor, open source"&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;meta name="rights" content="© 2026 DogsBay Ltd."&gt;</code>. The PDF transform uses the index terms to generate an index.</p>
      </Step>
      </Steps>
      <p>Test the metadata policy. Delete the <code>&lt;critdates&gt;</code> block from <em>Trimming audio</em> and run the gate:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"== project-health  /home/you/audacity-guide ==\nRoot map: audacity-guide.ditamap (project config); house rules: none (none configured)\nMetadata policy (1 of 21 files):\n  /home/you/audacity-guide/topics/trimming-audio.dita — [error] missing required \u003ccreated @date>\nUnused keys (3):\n  start-here  [/home/you/audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:26]\n  digital-audio  [/home/you/audacity-guide/audacity-guide.ditamap:33]\n  gl-normalization  [/home/you/audacity-guide/keydefs-glossary.ditamap:10]\n\nSummary\n  Metadata policy               1  in 1 of 21 files (1 error(s), 0 warning(s))\n    missing required \u003ccreated @date>                                  1\n  Unused keys                   3\nFAIL: project-health found issues"} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>The file is valid; <code>&lt;critdates&gt;</code> is optional to the DTD. The policy is what makes it required, for tasks, in this project.</p>
      <p>Undo the policy test, then test the element order. Move <code>&lt;resourceid&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;data&gt;</code> in <em>What is Audacity?</em> to before <code>&lt;metadata&gt;</code>, and validation fails:</p>
      <CodeBlock code={"== validate-project  /home/you/audacity-guide ==\n/home/you/audacity-guide/topics/what-is-audacity.dita:\n  29:12  error: The content of element type \"prolog\" does not match its content model.\n21 file(s): 20 valid, 1 invalid.\nFAIL: validation errors"} lang="plaintext" />
      <p>After each error exercise, undo the deliberate change and rerun the gate. Confirm that it prints <code>STAGE OK</code> before continuing.</p>
      <h2 id="what-you-learned" class="group scroll-mt-20">What you learned<a href="#what-you-learned" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
      <ul>
      <li><code>&lt;prolog&gt;</code> after <code>&lt;shortdesc&gt;</code>, with <code>&lt;author&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;copyright&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;critdates&gt;</code> (<code>&lt;created&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;revised&gt;</code>), <code>&lt;metadata&gt;</code> (<code>&lt;audience&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;category&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;keywords&gt;</code>), then <code>&lt;resourceid&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;data&gt;</code>, in that order.</li>
      <li><code>&lt;indexterm&gt;</code>, nested for sub-entries; <code>&lt;index-see&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;index-see-also&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;index-sort-as&gt;</code> inside an entry.</li>
      <li>A <code>&lt;glossgroup&gt;</code> and a shared topic are topics and carry prologs like any other.</li>
      <li>Map <code>&lt;topicmeta&gt;</code> takes the same elements for the publication.</li>
      <li>A metadata policy in <code>.dogsbay/config.xml</code>: <code>&lt;rule field presence topic-type pattern&gt;</code>, enforced by <code>project-health</code> and so by the gate.</li>
      <li>End of Part 2: a map with structure and a reltable, a key space, a shared topic, a glossary and metadata, published as one HTML5 deliverable.</li>
      </ul>
      <h2 id="next-lesson" class="group scroll-mt-20">Next lesson<a href="#next-lesson" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1" data-pagefind-ignore>&para;</a></h2>
